users "1" --> "0..1" cv_selections : owns explicit source selection
cv_selections --> cvs : validates owner and version
cv_upload_capacity --> cvs : reserves record and original capacity
note for cv_upload_capacity "One journaled CAS ledger; owner/global totals derived from at most 20,000 fixed-shape entries. File locks and generation checks fence publication/deletion; no TTL release of uncertain bytes."
note for cv_model_usage "Journaled daily provider-attempt admission across extraction, routing and clarification. Newer days reset counts; backwards clocks do not. Separate fixed OS-locked slots enforce owner/global concurrency."
users "1" --> "0..*" cv_conversations : owns private retained history
cv_conversations --> cvs : optional source reference
users "1" --> "0..1" career_state : owns current goal metadata
career_state --> career_goals : exact current goal reference
note for cvs "CV-owned structured evidence, overlays, interpretation and history. UUID IDs and private temporary originals; public reads expose no path or owner metadata."
note for cv_conversations "Nullable CV permits manual-only entry. Bounded messages/action receipts have separate transcript revisions; no automatic history expiry."
note for career_state "Automatic goal saving is distinct from explicit CV confirmation. Stamp binds goal ID/version, selection revision and projection hash. Changes invalidate it without another goal record or deleting CV facts."
note for career_goals "Older UUID reviewed-target documents remain retained history, excluded from canonical ObjectId reads. Canonical create_key metadata preserves the legacy uniqueness index; no destructive migration."
